fix(pkg): use an open-ended dsh engine range

Switches the declared range from a bounded form to `>=0.2.0-rc.2`, per the
tech-stack assessment's own recommendation (section 2.4). The host iterates
0.2.x-rc releases, so an open lower bound covers those without an edit here
on every host upgrade.

The trade-off is real and is now written down rather than left implicit: a
future 0.3.0 is accepted too, so a breaking change there would install and
misbehave instead of being reported as incompatible. When that happens the
range gets tightened and a patch released. scripts/verify-dsh-range.mjs
states this in its header and asserts both the accepted 0.2.x line and the
fact that 0.3.0/1.0.0 currently pass.

Also fills the last two gaps against the team template: LICENSE is listed
in files, and a test:watch script exists for development.
